{
  "title": "19th Night of Ramadhan",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "It is recommended to repeat the following imploration one hundred times on the nineteenth night of Ramadan:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللهَ رَبِّي وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهِ۔\nASTAGHFIRUL LAAHA RABBEE WA ATOOBU ILAYH.\nI implore Allah's forgiveness, my Lord, and I repent to Him.\nIt is also recommended to repeat the following imprecatory prayer one hundred times on the nineteenth night of Ramadan:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ الْعَنْ قَتَلَةَ اَمِيْرِ المُؤْمِنِيْنَ۔\nALLAAHUMMAL A'N QATALATA AMEERIL MU'MINEEN.\nO Allah, curse the slayers of the Commander of the Faithful.\nIt is recommended to say the aforementioned supplicatory prayer that begins with [\"Ya dhal-ladhi kana qabla kulli shay\"](AA19).\nIt is also recommended to say the following supplicatory prayer:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْ فِيْمَا تَقْضِيْ وَتُقَدِّرُ مِنَ الْاَمْرِ الْمَحْتُوْمِ وَفِيْمَا تَفْرُقُ مِنَ الْاَمْرِ الْحَكِيْمِ فِيْ لَيْلَةِ الْقَدْرِ وَفِي الْقَضَاۤءِ الَّذِيْ لَا يُرَدُّ وَلَا يُبَدَّلُ اَنْ تَكْتُبَنِيْ مِنْ حُجَّاجِ بَيْتِكَ الْحَرَامِ الْمَبْرُوْرِ حَجُّهُمُ الْمَشْكُوْرِ سَعْيُهُمُ، الْمَغْفُوْرِ ذُنُوْبُهُمُ، الْمُكَفَّرِ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّئَاتُهُمْ، وَاجْعَلْ فِيْمَا تَقْضِيْ وَتُقَدِّرُ اَنْ تُطِيْلَ عُمْرِيْ، وَتُوَسِّعَ عَلَيَّ فِي رِزْقِيْ، وَتَفْعَلَ بِيْ۔\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'L FEEMAA TAQDEE WA TUQADDIRU MINAL AMRIL MAHTOOMI WA FEEMAA TAFRUQU MINAL AMRIL HAKEEMI FEE LAYLATIL QADR, WA FIL QADAAA-IL LAZEE LAA YURADDU WA LAA YUBADDAL, AN TAKTUBANEE MIN HUJJAAJI BAYTIKAL HARAAMIL MABROORI HAJJUHUMUL MASHKOORI SA-I'YUHUM, AL-MAGHFOORI ZUNOOBUHUM, AL-MUKAFFARI A'NHUM SAYYI-AATUHUM, WAJ-A'L FEEMAA TAQDEE WA TUQADDIRU AN TUTEELA U'MREE, WA TUWASSI-A' A'LAYYA FEE RIZQEE, WA TAF-A'LA BEE.\nO Allah, decide, among what You decree and ordain from the decisive matter, and what You apportion from the wise command on the Night of Decree, and in the destiny that is not reversed nor changed, to inscribe me among the pilgrims of Your Sacred House - whose pilgrimage is accepted, whose effort is thanked, whose sins are forgiven, and whose bad deeds are absolved - and decide, among what You decree and ordain, to prolong my life, to expand my sustenance, and to do with me...\nOne may mention his desires after that."
}
